# Orkestr Travel — environment template.
#
# NAMES AND SAFE PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. Never commit a real value.
# Copy to `.env.local`, which is gitignored, and fill it in there.
#
# Rules (see docs/SECURITY.md):
#   * A secret must NEVER use the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — that prefix inlines the
#     value into the browser bundle at build time.
#   * Every integration is OPTIONAL. Nothing here is required to run the
#     deterministic core, the test suite, the production build, or the demo.
#     With this file empty the application runs in fixture mode and says so.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alibaba Cloud Model Studio (Qwen) — PHASE 6, implemented
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Powers structured intent extraction and bounded web research.
#
# With no key set the application does NOT break. The understanding and research
# screens replay hand-written fixture data and label it LOCAL FIXTURE. Nothing
# has ever been recorded from Model Studio, so nothing claims to have been.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE KILL SWITCH. Read this before setting anything else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# External calls are OFF unless this says so. A credential is a capability, not
# an instruction: leaving a key here must never be enough to make an accidental
# form submission spend money.
#
#   disabled  (default) Never touch the network. Fixtures serve every screen.
#   recorded            Never touch the network. Serve stored artefacts.
#   live                MAY call Model Studio, if credentials are also present.
#
# An unset, misspelt or unrecognised value means `disabled`. The safe reading of
# an unclear instruction is to do nothing.
#
# Check the current state at any time, with no network request and no secret in
# the output:   npm run preflight:model-studio
MODEL_STUDIO_MODE=disabled

# Server-side only. Never exposed to the browser; read in exactly one module
# (src/adapters/modelStudio/config.ts) and used in exactly one place, the
# Authorization header in src/adapters/modelStudio/transport.ts.
#
# Inert while MODEL_STUDIO_MODE is not `live`: the config reader returns before
# it reads this at all.
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=

# Your Model Studio workspace id, from the Workspace Details page in the
# console. It is account configuration, so it lives here and never in the repo.
MODEL_STUDIO_WORKSPACE_ID=

# Region for the OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Singapore is the default.
# Known values: ap-southeast-1, ap-northeast-1, cn-beijing, cn-hongkong,
# eu-central-1.
MODEL_STUDIO_REGION=ap-southeast-1

# Optional. Overrides the region + workspace endpoint entirely. Must be https.
# Useful if the endpoint host changes, or for a legacy shared domain.
DASHSCOPE_BASE_URL=

# Models. Environment-configurable on purpose: nothing is architected around
# one model name, and a more expensive model is never selected automatically.
QWEN_EXTRACTION_MODEL=qwen3.7-plus
QWEN_RESEARCH_MODEL=qwen3.7-plus

# How structured output is requested: json_object (default) or json_schema.
# Model Studio documents json_object for every Qwen model that supports
# structured output; its json_schema documentation is inconsistent between
# pages, so the unambiguous mode is the default. Either way the response is
# validated by src/core/intent/schema.ts, which is the real guarantee.
QWEN_STRUCTURED_OUTPUT_MODE=json_object

# Per-call deadline in milliseconds. 1–120000. Defaults to 30000.
MODEL_STUDIO_TIMEOUT_MS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Atlas flight provider — PHASE 7, implemented and live-verified
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THERE IS NO ATLAS API KEY HERE, AND THERE MUST NEVER BE ONE.
#
# The official `atlas-flight` CLI owns its own credentials in the operating
# system's secure store, obtained through a browser authorization the person
# performs themselves. This application never reads that store, never passes a
# token, and never puts one in a command argument. The CLI process IS the
# credential boundary.
#
# Setup is two commands the founder runs once, documented in
# docs/EXTERNAL_SETUP.md. Neither of them produces a value that belongs here.

# The kill switch, same shape as MODEL_STUDIO_MODE and the same default.
#
#   disabled  (default) The CLI is never started. Nothing reaches Atlas.
#   recorded            Replay a real, verified sandbox result from disk.
#   sandbox             Contact the Atlas sandbox, after proving the environment.
#
# There is deliberately NO `production` value. Production is not disabled by
# configuration in this application; it is absent from the type, so selecting it
# would require a code change and a review rather than an environment variable.
#
# Atlas itself defaults to PRODUCTION, which is why the adapter re-establishes
# sandbox immediately before every single call rather than trusting a setting.
ATLAS_MODE=disabled

# Optional per-call deadlines in milliseconds. 1000–300000.
# Defaults: search 90000, verify 60000.
ATLAS_SEARCH_TIMEOUT_MS=
ATLAS_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_MS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared trips — STAGE 3, implemented and live-verified
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lets a group open one trip from several devices, each person as themselves.
#
# ENTIRELY OPTIONAL. With DATABASE_URL unset the product is exactly what it was:
# local trips in the browser, explore, plan, what-if, the example. The sharing
# controls say sharing is not configured here. What they never do is appear to
# create an invite that nobody can use.
#
# Standard PostgreSQL and the standard driver. No provider SDK touches
# persistence, so moving between hosts is this one value rather than a rewrite.

# Server-side only. A connection string, never exposed to the browser -- a test
# asserts it appears in no bundle, and there is deliberately no NEXT_PUBLIC_
# variant of it.
#
# Percent-encode special characters in the password (@ -> %40, # -> %23,
# / -> %2F, : -> %3A, % -> %25). An unencoded @ splits the URL in the wrong
# place and shows up as "password authentication failed".
#
# Check it without printing it:   npm run db:check
DATABASE_URL=

# The absolute base for invite links, e.g. https://orkestr.example.
# Unset in development falls back to the request origin, which is correct for a
# localhost link. It is never guessed in production: a manufactured domain is
# how an organiser copies a link that points nowhere.
APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional off switch, for a demo or an incident where the right move is to
# stop writing. `disabled` turns shared trips off even where the database is
# reachable. Unset means on, if DATABASE_URL is present.
ORKESTR_SHARED_MODE=

# Schema is applied by a person, never on boot or on deploy:
#   npm run db:status     what has run, what has not
#   npm run db:migrate    apply what is pending

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS REQUIRED TO DEPLOY. With every value unset the
# application builds, serves every route, and runs the whole demo from recorded
# and fixture data — labelled as such on screen. See docs/DEPLOYMENT_PLAN.md.
